<script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/players/grant-nelson/#faq","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/players/grant-nelson/"},"mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What Is Grant Nelson’s Salary With the Nets?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Nelson earns $678.88k in 2026-27 on a two-way contract, with $91k guaranteed. He’s on identical terms to Tyler Bilodeau and almost identical terms to Chaney Johnson. He earned $73.15k last season from a single ten-day contract, which is the smallest published figure anywhere on this roster. Two-way pay sits outside Brooklyn‘s $160.06m payroll."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What’s Next for Grant Nelson Beyond 2026?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Nelson's two-way covers this season only and almost none of it is guaranteed. Converting to a standard contract would be the breakthrough, and another two-way the ordinary next step. He'll be 25 next summer."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How Much Does Grant Nelson Earn Over Time?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A $678.88k season is hard to picture, so here's what it comes to over smaller stretches of time."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What Are the Terms of Grant Nelson’s Contract?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Nelson signed a one-year two-way contract with Brooklyn on September 4, 2026 worth $678.88k with $91k guaranteed. It’s the third contract of his career. The two before it were a camp deal that didn’t convert and a ten-day in February, so this is the first arrangement that covers a whole season."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What Is Grant Nelson’s Net Worth?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Nelson’s net worth is estimated at around $300k, based on about $752k in published career earnings. No outlet publishes a figure for a player at this stage. Almost all of that is this season’s contract. He went undrafted out of Alabama in 2025 after four college seasons, having started at North Dakota State before transferring, so there was no rookie contract to begin with."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why Do the Nets Have Grant Nelson on a Two-Way Deal?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Nelson is on a two-way contract because he went undrafted, and a seven-footer without a draft position starts at the bottom like everyone else. A full season on a two-way is a considerable step up from ten days in February."}}]}</script>
